$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1.4 Mechanosynthesis of Stilbene (1b) Prior to use, styrene was passed
through a silica plug to remove peroxides or chemical stabilizers.
Styrene (1a, 230 µL, 2 mmol) was added to a 10 mL Teflon jar charged with
a single stainless steel ball bearing. A portion of catalyst D (3.0 mg,
0.25 mol%) was added to the jar. The reaction mixture was then milled for
a period of 15 minutes. Another portion of the catalyst was added to the
reaction mixture, which was then milled for an additional 15 minutes. The
catalyst was removed from the brown colored crude mixture, and the
resulting white solid was filtered and dried in air. White powder (97%
yield); 1H-NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.18 (s, 2H), δ 7.29-7.36 (m, 2H), δ
7.39- 7.46 (m, 4H), δ 7.56-7.61 (m, 4H) 13C-NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ
126.60, δ 127.69, δ 128.76, δ 137.40 HR-MS: calculated for C14H13 [M]:
181.1012; measured: 181.1010
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid state, incremental addition of catalyst, optimized on catalysts,
stainless steel ball used, no solvent
