$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Procedure for Ring-Closing Metathesis Reaction: Preparation of Compound 5
Grubbs’ first-generation catalyst (0.015 g, 0.02 mmol) was added to a
degassed solution of compound 6 (0.1 g, 0.38 mmol) in dichloromethane (50
mL), and the reaction mixture was stirred at ambient temperature under
nitrogen atmosphere for 5h. Solvent was removed, and the product was
chromatographed on silica gel. Elution with petroleum ether/ethyl acetate
(70:30) gave the product 5 (0.085g, 96%) as a colorless liquid. R f = 0.4
petroleum ether/ethyl acetate (80:20). IR (film) ν max: 2931, 1704, 1124
cm-1. 1H NMR (400MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.66-7.62 (m, 1H), 6.38 (superimposed dd,
J1 = J2 = 7.8Hz, 1H), 6.29 (superimposed dd with structure, J1 = J2 =
7.8Hz, 1H), 6.08 (dt, J1 = 5.8Hz, J2 = 2.1Hz, 1H), 4.01-3.80 (m, 4H),
3.57 (dt, J1 = 19.6Hz, J2 = 2.5Hz, 1H), 2.82-2.74 (m, 1H), 2.56 (dt, J1 =
19.6Hz, J2 = 2.5Hz, 1H), 2.38 (d, J = 6.6Hz, 1H), 1.88-1.72 (m, 2H), 1.48
(dd, J1 = 12.2Hz, J2 = 2.7Hz, 2H). 13C NMR (100MHz, CDCl3): δ 212.4,
162.3, 132.2, 131.9, 131.7, 112.9, 64.2, 63.1, 48.3, 45.5, 43.9, 40.3,
40.0, 31.4. HRMS (ESI): m/z [M + H]+ calcd. for C14H17O3: 233.1178;
found: 233.1168.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Ring-closing metathesis, key step
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
