$DATUM Mechanosynthesis of 2,5-Dihydro-1H-Pyrrolium Tetrafluoroborate (7b)
N,N-diallylammonium tetrafluoroborate (7a, 185.0 mg, 1 mmol) was added to
a 10 mL Teflon jar charged with a single stainless steel ball bearing.
150 wt. % NaCl and a portion of catalyst D (8.4 mg, 0.667 mol%) was added
to the jar. 50 µL of propylene carbonate was used as the LAG solvent. The
reaction mixture was then milled with a period of 30 minutes. After each
milling period, another portion of the catalyst was added to the reaction
mixture and milled for another period of time for a total of 1.5 hours of
milling time. The product was isolated and recrystallized from the brown
colored crude mixture by hot filtration using hot, anhydrous 1,4-dioxane,
and the resulting white solid was filtered and dried in air. White powder
(96% yield); 1H-NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 3.91 (s, 4H), δ 5.90 (s, 2H), δ
8.95 (s, 2H) 13C-NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 52.22, δ 125.65 HR-MS:
calculated for C4H8N [M]: 70.0651; measured: 70.0650
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM incremental addition of catalyst, stainless steel ball used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Mechanochemical Ruthenium-Catalyzed Olefin Metathesis
