$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N2 was bubbled through a solution of 2a (0.100 g, 0.070 mmol) and Grubbs
I (0.003 g, 0.004 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (70 mL) for 1 h. After this time,
ESI-MS indicated 69% reaction conversion. A further portion of Grubbs I
(0.003 g, 0.004 mmol) was added, and N2 was bubbled through for an
additional hour, at which time ESI-MS indicated the reaction had gone to
completion. The resulting solution was concentrated and passed through a
silica pad using CH2Cl2 as the eluent. [Rh(C^N^C-C12H22)(CO)][BArF 4] as
a yellow glass (cis:trans ~ 1:3). Yield: 0.096 g (95%). Data for
[Rh(C^N^C-C12H22)(CO)][BArF 4]: 1H NMR (400 MHz, CD2Cl2, trans isomer
only): δ 7.88 (t, 3JHH = 7.7, 1H, py), 7.70-7.75 (m, 8H, ArF), 7.55 (br,
4H, ArF), 7.50 (d, 3JHH = 7.7, 2H, py), 7.15 (d, 3JHH = 1.9, 2H, imid),
7.01 (d, 3JHH = 1.9, 2H, imid), 5.40 (br, 2H, pyCH2), 5.35-5.39 (m,
2H,CH=CH), 5.03 (br, 2H, pyCH2), 3.90-4.36 (m, 4H, N-CH2CH2), 1.14-2.24
(m, 16H, CH2). ESI-MS (CH3CN, 180 °C, 3 kV): positive ion: 534.1762 m/z,
[M]+ (calcd. 534.1735).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Ring-closing metathesis, incremental addition of first generation Grubbs
catalyst, product obtained as a mixture of 1:3 cis:trans isomers
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Reactivity of NHC-Based Rhodium Macrocycles
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Andrew, Rhiann E.; Chaplin, Adrian B.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Inorganic Chemistry (2015), 54(1), 312-322

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME328 STEP1
